            <ArticleTitle>[Incidence of orthostatic hypotension. Clinical study on 1010 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3395-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An investigation conducted on a series of 1010 patients selected without regard to age, sex, or pathology showed that orthostatic hypotension is very common (about 35%), especially in aged and hypertensive subjects. It was found that cardiovascular causes play a by no means unimportant part in its determination. Only 20% of the cases observed were attributable to drug treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
